The accidental release prevention and emergency response policies:
Savage Infrastructure LLC (Savage) is strongly committed to managing the Safety, Health and Environmental risks of the chemicals at our sites.
We demonstrate our responsibility for the safety of our Team Members, our Customers, Partners, the public, and the environment through safe work practices and regulatory compliance;
Well achieve our goal of zero incidents when every Team Member practices safety as a core value and works safely in every circumstance;
We praise safe behavior and strive to identify and correct unsafe acts or unsafe conditions;
Every Savage Team Member is obligated to stop work if we observe unsafe acts or conditions that could result in an injury, fatality, or damage to facilities or equipment;
Were committed to maintaining safety standards that meet or exceed customer, federal, state and local requirements; and
All Team Members must use safe work procedures and practices in doing our work.
It is Savage's policy to adhere to all applicable Federal, State and local rules and regulations, as well as industry standards and best practices. As part of this commitment, Savage has established a system to help ensure safe operation of the processes at this facility that includes the prevention of accidental releases of hazardous substances. One component of this system is a Risk Management Program (RMP) that complies with the requirements of the Environmental Protection Agency's (EPA's) regulation under 40 CFR Part 68. The site is also subject to the Occupational Safety & Health Administration's (OSHA's) Process Safety Management (PSM) Standard, 29 CFR 1910.119.
Savage maintains a Safety, Health and Environmental Policy Manual that sites must comply with regardless of RMP/PSM applicability. The policies are intended to ensure our sites are operated safely and that all Team Members and contractors perform their tasks in a safe and responsible manner.
