e operating procedures for the movement and storage of railcars as well as performing track inspections per FRA regulations. These key elements of the prevention program are supported by the development and collection of up-to-date process safety information.
Our day-to-day activities are governed by our safe work practices, hot work, and contractor management policies and procedures.  Savage promotes a lesson learning environment and strives for continuous improvement with processes in place for incident investigation, management of change, pre-startup safety review, and compliance auditing.
Savage encourages Team Member participation in all aspects of the PSM/RMP Program elements. Team Members consultation and participation are sought and achieved through various methods including:
 Integrating PSM/RMP activities into regular work activities;
 Consulting with affected Team Members;
 Consulting with Team Members representatives;
 Compiling and providing access to PSM/RMP information;
 Incident and near miss reporting;
 Participation in the safety committees, including participation through the Safety Specialist and Lead Safety Specialist Programs; and
 Providing comments and suggestions on any aspect of the Process Safety and Risk Management Program.
The five-year accident history:
Savage has not had any releases that meet the RMP five-year accident history criteria.
The emergency response program:
The Tooele facility has a written Emergency Action Plan that has been developed to meet the emergency planning, response and notification requirements of the EPA and OSHA regulations. This plan outlines the responsibilities and actions required to control an emergency specific to the types of incidents that could occur at the site.
